Breadth-First Search (BFS) in Python
📘 Description

Breadth-First Search (BFS) is a graph traversal algorithm used to explore nodes level by level. It starts from a source node and visits all neighboring nodes before moving to the next depth level. BFS is commonly used in graphs, trees, shortest path problems, AI search techniques, and networking.

✨ Characteristics of BFS
🔹 Traverses nodes level-wise
🔹 Uses a Queue (FIFO) data structure
🔹 Finds the shortest path in an unweighted graph
🔹 Visits each node only once
🔹 Suitable for graphs and tree structures
🔹 Time Complexity: O(V + E)
V → Vertices
E → Edges
⚙️ Working Process of BFS

1️⃣ Start from the source node.
2️⃣ Mark the node as visited ✔️
3️⃣ Insert the node into the queue 📥
4️⃣ Remove a node from the queue 📤
5️⃣ Visit all unvisited neighboring nodes 🌐
6️⃣ Repeat until the queue becomes empty 🔚
